  "literature_notes": "KCNA3/Kv1.3 has a large intracellular N-terminal domain (residues 1\u2013234) and an intracellular C-terminal domain (residues 478\u2013575). Every tag in the ledger lands in one of these intracellular regions. L1/L2 (PMC5973702): C-terminal FLAG/10Xhis tag \u2014 C-terminus is residue 575, within the intracellular span 478\u2013575; disqualified as intracellular. L2 also mentions an antibody recognising 'the first extracellular loop epitope' (EC1, residues 255\u2013296), but this is antibody epitope mapping, not a tag insertion \u2014 explicitly excluded by the rules. L3/L4/L5 (PMC4497498): eGFP fused 'immediately after the start codon' of full-length Kv1.3 \u2014 residue 1 is the first residue of the intracellular N-terminal domain; disqualified as intracellular (function was confirmed preserved, but the tag faces the cytoplasm). L6/L7 (DOI:10.1101/2024.01.29.577122 / PMC12989817): TurboID-V5 fused to both the 5' (N-terminal) and 3' (C-terminal) ends of Kcna3 \u2014 both termini are intracellular; disqualified. L8 (PMC12205523): GFP placed at the N-terminus via pEGFP-C2 vector \u2014 again the intracellular N-terminus; disqualified. No ledger line reports a tolerated tag insertion at any extracellular position of KCNA3. The three extracellular loops (EC1: 255\u2013296, EC2: 342\u2013369, EC3: 420\u2013455) are unaddressed by any qualifying insertion in the ledger. Zero sites is the correct answer.",
